Lead City University
Cyber Security Programme ? 400 Level
Participant: THOMAS GODSLOVE
Track: Data Analytics
Training Dates: 27 ? 31 October 2025

------------------------------------------------------------
1. Background
------------------------------------------------------------

The university hosted a collaborative boot camp with the CADD Centre to help final-year students convert theory into practice. I enrolled in the Data Analytics pathway, where Mr. Patrick guided us through a progressive blend of classroom instruction, spreadsheet labs, and presentation drills. The following pages document the structure, the sequence of activities, and the competencies gained.

------------------------------------------------------------
2. Daily Learning Log
------------------------------------------------------------

Day 1 ? Foundations of Analytics
- Defined data types and their organisational value; compared qualitative vs. quantitative and discrete vs. continuous datasets.
- Outlined the analytics project lifecycle: collecting, cleaning, exploring, visualising, and delivering recommendations.
- Navigated Microsoft Excel beyond basics, reinforcing cell references and using autofill, conditional formatting, and summary functions (SUM, AVERAGE, COUNTA, MAX, MIN) on sample tables.

Day 2 ? Working Smarter with Excel
- Moved into text-handling formulas such as LEFT/RIGHT, CONCAT, and TEXTJOIN for quick data preparation.
- Practised logical expressions (IF, IFS, AND/OR combinations) to model business rules within spreadsheets.
- Explored lookup strategies including VLOOKUP, XLOOKUP, and INDEX/MATCH for pulling targeted records from wider tables.
- Closed with an introduction to SQL concepts to highlight how analysts query structured datasets at scale.

Day 3 ? Data Cleaning Sprint
- Received a fictional sales workbook and performed structured cleaning: fixing typos, standardising formats, and handling blanks.
- Applied data validation and filters to enforce consistency before analysis.
- Reflected on the industry reality that preparation consumes most analyst hours and determines result quality.

Day 4 ? Insight Generation & Visual Storytelling
- Leveraged the cleansed dataset to build PivotTables summarising performance by geography, product category, and sales agent.
- Produced charts (clustered columns, line graphs, pie charts) tied to management questions such as ?Which region leads growth?? and ?What products drive revenue??
- Drafted talking points that linked each visual to an actionable recommendation for stakeholders.

Day 5 ? Presentations and Career Guidance
- Transformed findings into a compact Excel dashboard, assembling slicers, KPIs, and explanatory captions.
- Presented a walkthrough of the dashboard and fielded feedback as if addressing a department head.
- Participated in a Q&A on analytics career paths, further certifications, and how to combine Excel skills with SQL and Power BI for professional roles.

------------------------------------------------------------
3. Competency Gains
------------------------------------------------------------

- Project Workflow Awareness: Can map each stage of the analytics lifecycle and allocate time/resources accordingly.
- Spreadsheet Proficiency: Confident using intermediate/advanced Excel features (logical functions, lookups, PivotTables) to resolve business questions.
- Data Quality Mindset: Able to design cleaning steps and articulate why trustworthy data is the prerequisite for insight.
- Visual Communication: Selects charts that fit the story and frames results in language useful to decision makers.
- Professional Readiness: Strengthened presentation skills and gained clarity on next steps for a data analytics career.

------------------------------------------------------------
4. Closing Reflection
------------------------------------------------------------

The Data Analytics boot camp condensed a wide skill set into five productive days. The format?concepts in the morning, labs after lunch, feedback at close?ensured retention and constant application. I intend to extend the learning by rebuilding the dashboard with new datasets and deepening my SQL knowledge. I appreciate Lead City University and Mr. Patrick for creating a platform that advances my readiness for data-driven roles.
